S127 LRC14 TOURNAMENT-REALIZABILITY SUMMIT ATLAS
========================================================================
[Assumption challenge]
  considered vertex sets:
    runners/speeds, residues, gaps, fixed circle sections, section boundaries,
    wall-crossing events, cover arcs, Fourier modes, matroid/cycle circuits,
    and proof obligations/filters.
  chosen here:
    Z/14 apex points and denominator-14 runner phases, because these preserve
    the exact half-clock cutoff where AP/GW bind.
  challenged assumption:
    raw runner tournaments are not enough.  The residue-liar and Farey
    near-miss can share coarse winding data with tight rows while q(S) and
    off-apex M separate them.  A proof must state both the tournament
    realizability theorem and the arithmetic data the quotient intentionally
    forgets.

[Apex-clock tournament realizability]
  vertices: seven selected points on Z/14Z
  observable: clockwise displacement
  switch/gauge: x->y iff 0 < y-x < 7; diameter/collision ties either excluded or
    broken by the Hamiltonian path induced by increasing residue
  quotient preserves: half-clock order class and diameter-tie count
  quotient destroys: actual speed divisibility, runner labels, off-apex M

  tie_policy=exclude: labelled rows=128, isomorphism classes=10
